Package: ONgeoRapp
Title: Shiny Application for Ontario Geography Linking with 'ONgeoR'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Lennon", "Li", email = "lennon.yeli@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Steven", "Johnson", role = "aut"))
Description: Provides the interactive Shiny application companion to the
    'ONgeoR' package. Users pick a source layer and a target layer from the
    Ontario Land Information Ontario (LIO) registry, and the geometry pair
    alone determines the linking operation (polygon intersection, nearest
    point matching, containment, or raster sampling) with no rule for the
    user to choose. The application renders both layers on a map, shows the
    resulting linked table, and exports the mapping, pair table, map, and a
    reproducer script. Data is retrieved at runtime by 'ONgeoR'; none is
    bundled here.
